# Editor / IDE
.vscode/

# LUME-ACE3P run artifacts. A run leaves these wherever it is invoked, so running an
# example inside a checkout otherwise fills `git status` with output files — which is
# how test debris nearly got committed. The test suite itself runs in pytest's
# tmp_path; these cover a run started by hand.
sim_output.txt
sweep_output.txt
xopt_state.yml
*.rejected
*.rejected.[0-9]*
DRY_RUN.txt
lume_ace3p_state.json
gp_parameters.txt
Binary_gp_model.pt
inversion_result.txt
identifiability.txt
posterior_samples.txt
posterior_summary.txt
train_report.txt
lume-ace3p_*workdir*/
lume-ace3p_workflow_output*/

# ...but the frozen baselines are these same filenames, committed on purpose. Without
# this, re-freezing a baseline whose output is named `sim_output.txt` would silently
# skip it on `git add`.
!tests/baseline/**
